{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX 0xa5 with divider 64 never sets recv_buf_valid, so window ends with TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received and tohost FAIL 0xdead instead of echoed 0xa5/PASS. CONE_SLICE is unresolved (coverage 0/1, only spiflash.v:52/system.v refs) so trace+excerpt win per guard. Root cause at picosoc/simpleuart.v:39 where `reg [3:1] recv_state` gives only 3 bits (max 7 states) and cannot encode the full start+8-data+stop RX sequence, stalling the receiver FSM.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,1 +39,1 @@
-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;", "expected": "tohost PASS, received byte 0xa5, no TRAP: uart timeout"}

